# boot-title: start the game and capture the opening screens. No keys are sent until the copy
# protection prompt, which the script then leaves unanswered (it ends the run when the game waits).
# Virtual time: 1 BIOS tick = 1/18.2 s of the oracle's clock (1,000,000 instructions per second).
# Pin the time of day the program reads when it calls Randomize, so the random sequence (and
# the wheel question) never depends on how many instructions ran before it. The value is what the
# unpinned run produces, so recorded behaviour is unchanged.
clock 12:00:16.58
wait 440
shot ssi-logo            # SSI presents the Advanced Dungeons & Dragons computer product
wait 200
shot title               # POOL OF RADIANCE title picture
wait 160
shot credits             # scenario and game credits
